/tank/dregg-build/nanodregg/logs/gates11-commit20j-3.log:105:    **Why.** Ember, 10-21: "we don't need to focus on landings as much, as long as every now and then we make sure the whole system still builds and passes its tests, and do convergences at those points instead of EVERY LANDING." The numbers before (GATES-10, hbox logs/gates10-fluid-measure.out and the landing logs): **61 re-judges in 24 h for 57 landings**, each a full judge (every target, the census, every selected row, the waste, the generated files, the Rust workspace with clippy); a standing pass **41 min** (fc4022d); GATES-20b′'s own landing **~2.5 h through the queue**, displaced twice, and refused once by a **30-min slot starvation** that read `REFUSED by scripts/pre-push`; on 10-21 evening all four slots were held by full judges for **45 min straight** (ROOT), and this lane's own first two plant judges waited 30 min each and got no slot (the second already printing NOT JUDGED, item 6). GATES-20j itself (a 3-file `gates:` change): judged GREEN, displaced; GREEN, displaced; then REFUSED by the 30-min slot wait, ~2 h after launch, with nothing wrong in it. Of 60 landings in the 24 h to cdd9d84, 7 were flag days and 8 changed the judge's code (7 of them GATES' own); the other ~45 were judged in full for changes the next standing judged again anyway.
